        "html": "<h3>A chance meeting</h3>\n<p>Daniel runs into Maya at a coffee shop. He is waiting for his coffee when she calls his name.</p>\n<p><strong>Part A — Seeing each other again</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Maya:</strong> Daniel? Is that you?</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> Maya! Wow, long time no see.</p>\n<p><strong>Maya:</strong> I know. It&#39;s been ages. How have you been?</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> Pretty good, actually. I moved back to the neighborhood last month.</p>\n<p><strong>Maya:</strong> Really? I thought you were still living in Seattle.</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> I was, but I left my old job two years ago. I work from home now, so I can live pretty much anywhere.</p>\n<p><strong>Maya:</strong> That&#39;s a big change. Do you like being back?</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> So far, yes. The area is really different now, though. This coffee shop used to be a bookstore.</p>\n<p><strong>Maya:</strong> That&#39;s right. I used to spend hours there on weekends.</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> Are you still working at the hospital?</p>\n<p><strong>Maya:</strong> Yes, but I don&#39;t work on the wards anymore. I moved into staff training last year.</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> That makes sense. You were always good at explaining things.</p>\n<p><strong>Part B — Catching up and saying goodbye</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Maya:</strong> Thanks. What about your photography? Do you still take pictures?</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> Not as much as I used to, but I still take some on weekends.</p>\n<p><strong>Barista:</strong> Large coffee for Daniel!</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> That&#39;s me. Listen, I have to get going, but we should really catch up.</p>\n<p><strong>Maya:</strong> Definitely. Are you free sometime next week?</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> I think so. Let me check my schedule and get back to you.</p>\n<p><strong>Maya:</strong> Sounds good. It was really nice seeing you.</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> You too. And this time, let&#39;s not wait another eight years.</p>\n<h3>Check the story</h3>\n<p>先不要看译文，回答下面的问题：</p>\n<ol>\n<li>What made it possible for Daniel to move back?</li>\n<li>What used to be in the coffee shop&#39;s location?</li>\n<li>Does Maya still work on the hospital wards?</li>\n<li>What does Maya ask Daniel about?</li>\n<li>Do they make an exact plan to meet again?</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n"
