        "html": "<h3>Two details do not match</h3>\n<p>Daniel picks up lunch from Pine Street Deli. He checks the bag before leaving because the order is for him and Aisha.</p>\n<h3>Part A — Checking the order</h3>\n<p><strong>Clerk:</strong> Pickup for Daniel?</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> That&#39;s me. Thanks. Let me check the order before I go.</p>\n<p><strong>Clerk:</strong> Sure.</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> I&#39;m sorry to bother you, but there seems to be a mistake. This isn&#39;t what I ordered.</p>\n<p><strong>Clerk:</strong> Oh, I&#39;m sorry. What did you order?</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> I ordered one vegetable sandwich without cheese and one chicken sandwich. I got two chicken sandwiches.</p>\n<p><strong>Clerk:</strong> You&#39;re right. The label says one vegetable sandwich, no cheese.</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> I was also expecting a bottle of still water, but this is sparkling water.</p>\n<p><strong>Clerk:</strong> I see both errors on the receipt. We can replace the sandwich and the water.</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> Could you fix that, please? Aisha is waiting upstairs.</p>\n<p><strong>Clerk:</strong> Of course. The sandwich will take about six minutes. The water will only take a moment.</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> Okay. How long will the whole order take?</p>\n<p><strong>Clerk:</strong> No more than seven minutes.</p>\n<h3>Part B — Confirming the correction</h3>\n<p><strong>Clerk:</strong> Daniel? Here is the vegetable sandwich without cheese and one bottle of still water. Could you check them?</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> Vegetable, no cheese; still water. Yes, that&#39;s right. Thanks for helping me out.</p>\n<p><strong>Clerk:</strong> I&#39;m sorry about the mix-up.</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> No problem. You fixed it quickly. I owe you one—well, not literally. It was your order to fix.</p>\n<p><strong>Clerk:</strong> Fair point. Happy to help, anyway.</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> Thanks. Now I can take lunch upstairs before Aisha calls to ask where it is.</p>\n<h3>Check the story</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Why does Daniel check the bag before leaving?</li>\n<li>What sandwich did he order, and what did he get?</li>\n<li>What water did he expect, and what did he receive?</li>\n<li>How will the clerk solve both problems?</li>\n<li>How long will the whole correction take?</li>\n<li>Why does Daniel correct his own use of <strong>I owe you one</strong>?</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n"
