        "html": "<h3>Moving Lena&#39;s appointment</h3>\n<p>Lena has a haircut appointment at Northside Salon on Thursday afternoon. A work orientation has been extended, so she calls the salon.</p>\n<h3>Part A — Finding another time</h3>\n<p><strong>Receptionist:</strong> Northside Salon. How can I help?</p>\n<p><strong>Lena:</strong> Hi, I&#39;m calling about my appointment with Rosa on Thursday at four thirty. It&#39;s under Lena Ortiz.</p>\n<p><strong>Receptionist:</strong> Let me check. Yes, I see it here.</p>\n<p><strong>Lena:</strong> My work schedule has changed. Can I move my appointment?</p>\n<p><strong>Receptionist:</strong> Certainly. Rosa has an opening at five on Thursday.</p>\n<p><strong>Lena:</strong> The earliest I can do is five thirty. Do you have anything available after that?</p>\n<p><strong>Receptionist:</strong> Not on Thursday. She has eleven twenty or two forty on Friday.</p>\n<p><strong>Lena:</strong> Friday at eleven twenty works for me.</p>\n<p><strong>Receptionist:</strong> Great. I&#39;ll move it to Friday, the eleventh, at eleven twenty.</p>\n<p><strong>Lena:</strong> Just to check, that&#39;s Friday at eleven twenty with Rosa, right?</p>\n<p><strong>Receptionist:</strong> That&#39;s right.</p>\n<h3>Part B — Closing the loop</h3>\n<p><strong>Lena:</strong> Could you confirm the new time by text?</p>\n<p><strong>Receptionist:</strong> Yes. It should arrive in a moment. Your reference number will stay the same.</p>\n<p><strong>Lena:</strong> Thank you. Should I use the same front entrance?</p>\n<p><strong>Receptionist:</strong> Yes. Please arrive five minutes early.</p>\n<p><strong>Lena:</strong> Got it: Friday at eleven twenty, with Rosa, and I should arrive by eleven fifteen.</p>\n<p><strong>Receptionist:</strong> Exactly. Is there anything else I can help with?</p>\n<p><strong>Lena:</strong> No, that&#39;s everything. Thanks for your help.</p>\n<p><strong>Receptionist:</strong> You&#39;re welcome. See you Friday.</p>\n<p>Lena receives the text before ending the call. She compares it with her notes: the date, time, stylist and reference number all match.</p>\n<p>On Friday, Lena arrives at 11:15 and completes the appointment at the confirmed time. The rescheduling does not leave a future commitment for another lesson.</p>\n<h3>Check the story</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>What is Lena&#39;s original appointment time?</li>\n<li>Why does she need to move it?</li>\n<li>Why does the first alternative not work?</li>\n<li>What two Friday openings does the receptionist offer?</li>\n<li>What is the final appointment?</li>\n<li>What four details does Lena confirm before ending the call?</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n"
