        "id": "section-2",
        "title": "2. Main Conversation",
        "html": "<h3>A change at Riverton Central</h3>\n<p>Daniel and Aisha are taking the 10:20 train to Harbor City for a weekend design and photography fair. Their host expects them at noon.</p>\n<h3>Part A — Reading the change</h3>\n<p><strong>Aisha:</strong> The board has changed. The train&#39;s been delayed.</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> Do we know how long the delay is?</p>\n<p><strong>Aisha:</strong> Thirty-five minutes. The new departure time is 10:55, and the estimated arrival is 12:05.</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> The platform number is flashing too.</p>\n<p><strong>Aisha:</strong> Yes. The departure has been moved to Platform 7. Platform 4 is closed for maintenance.</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> Good catch. I was looking at the time, not the platform.</p>\n<h3>Part B — Comparing the options</h3>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> What are our options?</p>\n<p><strong>Aisha:</strong> We can wait for the direct train, or take the 10:35 local and change at East Gate.</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> When would the local route arrive?</p>\n<p><strong>Aisha:</strong> At 12:20, if the connection is on time.</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> Is the 10:35 local definitely on time?</p>\n<p><strong>Aisha:</strong> It is right now, but the connection at East Gate is only eight minutes.</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> That&#39;s not much time if the station is busy.</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> Then waiting is still faster, and we won&#39;t have to change trains with our bags.</p>\n<p><strong>Aisha:</strong> Agreed. I&#39;ll let our host know. How about: “Our train has been delayed by thirty-five minutes. We&#39;re staying on the direct service and should arrive at 12:05.”</p>\n<p><strong>Daniel:</strong> Add the new platform in case she checks the train status.</p>\n<p><strong>Aisha:</strong> Done. Now let&#39;s go to Platform 7.</p>\n<p>They reach the new platform before boarding begins. Their host replies that 12:05 still works.</p>\n<p>The direct train arrives at 12:05. Daniel and Aisha meet the host and attend the fair; the delay update is fully closed.</p>\n<h3>Check the story</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>What was the original departure time?</li>\n<li>How long is the delay?</li>\n<li>What are the new departure and estimated arrival times?</li>\n<li>Why has the platform changed?</li>\n<li>What is the alternative route?</li>\n<li>Why do Daniel and Aisha decide to wait?</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n"
