        "id": "section-2",
        "title": "2. Main Conversation",
        "html": "<h3>Choosing a workable solution</h3>\n<p>Lena and a conference colleague arrive at the Harbor Hotel at 3:20 p.m. Her confirmation says check-in begins at 3:00, and she has an online call at 3:30. Lena handles the conversation at the desk.</p>\n<h3>Part A — The problem</h3>\n<p><strong>Front desk agent:</strong> Welcome. How can I help?</p>\n<p><strong>Lena:</strong> Hi. We have a reservation under Lena Ortiz for a standard room with a desk.</p>\n<p><strong>Front desk agent:</strong> I found it. I&#39;m sorry, but the room isn&#39;t ready yet. Housekeeping has been delayed.</p>\n<p><strong>Lena:</strong> I understand, but we were told it would be ready by three. I have an online call in ten minutes.</p>\n<p><strong>Front desk agent:</strong> I&#39;m sorry about that. We can offer two options.</p>\n<p><strong>Lena:</strong> Before we decide, is there somewhere we can leave our bags?</p>\n<p><strong>Front desk agent:</strong> Yes. Luggage storage is beside the front desk.</p>\n<h3>Part B — Comparing the options</h3>\n<p><strong>Front desk agent:</strong> You can wait for the original room, which should be ready by four. Or we can offer another room now. It&#39;s quieter, but it doesn&#39;t have a desk.</p>\n<p><strong>Lena:</strong> If we wait, when will it be ready at the latest?</p>\n<p><strong>Front desk agent:</strong> By four. You may use the work lounge for your call.</p>\n<p><strong>Lena:</strong> Where is the lounge?</p>\n<p><strong>Front desk agent:</strong> Take the elevator to the second floor and follow the signs for the courtyard. The lounge is across from the elevator.</p>\n<p><strong>Lena:</strong> We&#39;d prefer to keep the original room because we need the desk. We&#39;ll store the bags and use the lounge until four.</p>\n<p><strong>Front desk agent:</strong> That works. I&#39;ll text you as soon as the room is ready.</p>\n<p><strong>Lena:</strong> Could you confirm that the room still has a desk?</p>\n<p><strong>Front desk agent:</strong> Yes—standard room, courtyard side, with a desk.</p>\n<p>At 3:52, Lena receives the text, finishes her call and checks in. The promised solution is completed in this lesson.</p>\n<h3>Check the story</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>What time does Lena arrive?</li>\n<li>What did the confirmation say about check-in?</li>\n<li>Why does Lena need a solution quickly?</li>\n<li>What are the two room options?</li>\n<li>Why does she keep the original room?</li>\n<li>When does she receive the room-ready text?</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n"
