        "html": "<h3>本课负荷说明</h3>\n<p>本课有5项全新主动表达：第1—5项。第6—10项整合前面学过的故障、时间和确认语言。</p>\n<h3>1. I locked myself out.</h3>\n<p>我把自己锁在外面了。<strong>myself</strong> 表示动作结果回到说话者本人。</p>\n<h3>2. I&#39;m outside …</h3>\n<p>我在……外面。后接具体、可找到的位置。</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I&#39;m outside the Pine Street entrance.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>3. I left my keys inside.</h3>\n<p>我把钥匙落在里面了。<strong>left</strong> 说明过去发生的原因。</p>\n<h3>4. The door closed behind me.</h3>\n<p>我出来后门在身后关上了。简洁说明事件经过。</p>\n<h3>5. Could someone let me in?</h3>\n<p>可以派人让我进去吗？请求授权帮助，不是请求绕过安全程序。</p>\n<h3>6. I&#39;ve already tried calling …</h3>\n<p>复现第23课的“已试步骤”，说明谁已联系以及结果。</p>\n<h3>7. How long will that take?</h3>\n<p>复现第14课，询问解决时间。</p>\n<h3>8. My battery is at … percent.</h3>\n<p>手机只剩……电。电量会影响沟通时才说明。</p>\n<h3>9. Is there any information you need?</h3>\n<p>还需要什么信息吗？让接听者补足处理所需字段。</p>\n<h3>10. So someone should be here in …, right?</h3>\n<p>复述预计时间并确认。<strong>should</strong> 表示合理预计，不是绝对保证。</p>\n<h3>Don&#39;t Say It That Way</h3>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>容易说出的句子</th>\n<th>更自然的表达</th>\n<th>原因</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>I locked out.</td>\n<td>I locked myself out.</td>\n<td>需要反身代词说明自己陷入该状态</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>I&#39;m here.</td>\n<td>I&#39;m outside the Pine Street entrance.</td>\n<td>陌生接听者需要可找到的位置</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Open door.</td>\n<td>Could someone let me in?</td>\n<td>请求授权帮助</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>I tried everything.</td>\n<td>I&#39;ve already tried calling my neighbor.</td>\n<td>只列出真实、安全的步骤</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n"
