        "html": "<h3>A. 理解检查</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Daniel has his building fob with him.</li>\n<li>He is outside the Pine Street main entrance.</li>\n<li>Aisha is available to let him in.</li>\n<li>Daniel tries to force the door.</li>\n<li>He has photo ID.</li>\n<li>The worker arrives in less than twenty-five minutes.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>B. 四类信息</h3>\n<p>把句子标为 <strong>event / location / tried / request</strong>：</p>\n<ol>\n<li>The door closed behind me.</li>\n<li>I&#39;m beside the north parking entrance.</li>\n<li>I&#39;ve called the after-hours number twice.</li>\n<li>Could an authorized worker meet me?</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>C. 修复无效消息</h3>\n<p>把“Hi, help me, I&#39;m outside”改写为45—65词的可处理语音消息。必须包含姓名、地点、经过、一个安全尝试、当前请求和可保持联系的方式。</p>\n<h3>D. 未知追问</h3>\n<p>伙伴扮演陌生接听者，随机追问：入口、姓名、是否有身份证件、已联系谁、手机电量。没有的信息不能编造；可以说 <strong>I don&#39;t know / I don&#39;t have that with me</strong>。</p>\n<h3>E. Lesson 20结转检索</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>A printer was promised by 2:00, but it is incomplete. Refer to the promised time.</li>\n<li>At a venue, ask for a place to store your group&#39;s bags.</li>\n<li>Your assigned room is unusable. Ask whether another room can be offered.</li>\n<li>Ask when the original room will be available if your group waits.</li>\n<li>After comparing two options, state that your group favors the quieter one.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>F. Lesson 22间隔检索</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Give a gentle suggestion that a friend have a repeating noise inspected.</li>\n<li>Suggest bringing a written timeline as a low-pressure good idea.</li>\n<li>Clearly recommend contacting a qualified professional because a problem has continued.</li>\n<li>The service desk closes in five minutes. Give time-sensitive advice with a consequence.</li>\n<li>Connect a repeated problem to the next action with an if-clause.</li>\n<li>Admit you cannot identify the cause, then give a limited next step.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>G. Unit 6无提示检索</h3>\n<p>合上第21—23课。下面18题分别检索三课的18项全新主动词块。</p>\n<ol>\n<li>A sore throat began five days ago and continues today. State the duration.</li>\n<li>Give the exact beginning: Sunday evening.</li>\n<li>Say the symptom has been more severe from Tuesday until now.</li>\n<li>Explain that it becomes worse whenever you speak for a long time.</li>\n<li>Report that you have experienced no fever.</li>\n<li>Close by saying you have reported every change you observed.</li>\n<li>Gently suggest that a repeating non-emergency problem be professionally inspected.</li>\n<li>Suggest writing down the times as a low-pressure good idea.</li>\n<li>Give a clear recommendation to contact the appropriate qualified service.</li>\n<li>The office closes now; give a strong, time-sensitive recommendation.</li>\n<li>Begin a condition about a fault that continues to recur.</li>\n<li>Admit that you cannot identify the cause, then continue with a safe next step.</li>\n<li>State that a wireless connection repeatedly disconnects.</li>\n<li>Say the fault occurs at thirty-minute intervals.</li>\n<li>Tell support you have previously attempted a restart.</li>\n<li>Report two troubleshooting actions in order.</li>\n<li>Say the fault continues despite those actions.</li>\n<li>Ask support for the next action to attempt.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>H. Unit 5—6跨单元累计任务</h3>\n<p>完成一次“去陌生地点处理突发问题”的90—120秒任务。必须明确调用L17、L18、L19、L20各至少一项词块，再加入本单元的症状或故障描述：请求公共空间许可、确认路线、处理延误、解决服务问题，最后说明当前故障和请求。目标词块必须由你主动检索，不能看答案拼接。</p>\n<hr>\n"
